Subject: Stage 3 Escalation =E2=80=93 Systemic Equality-Law Breach and Administra=
tive Deflection (CA-2024-001342 / BV20D01752)

=20

Dear Mr Goodwin, Dr Farrar, Ms Sackman MP and Ms Davies-Jones MP,

=20

Please find attached my Stage 3 escalation letter concerning the continuing=
 failure of HMCTS and the Ministry of Justice to address my Pre-Action corre=
spondence of 20 and 21 October 2025 and subsequent escalations on 28 and 29 =
October 2025.

=20

Despite multiple written submissions, neither department has provided ackno=
wledgment or a substantive reply.  Instead, the matter has been repeatedly m=
isclassified as a =E2=80=9Cjudicial=E2=80=9D issue, preventing any administrative or equ=
ality-law review.  This deflection is itself an administrative failure and b=
reaches the Public Sector Equality Duty under s.149 Equality Act 2010.

=20

The attached letter summarises:
The unlawful revocation of participation measures post-trial in breach of F=
PR Part 3A;
The mischaracterisation of autism-related behaviour as misconduct (see para=
graph 64 of the judgment 18 April 2024);
The procedural exclusion that followed when my disabilities (autism and PTS=
D) were ignored; and
The systemic deflection of equality-law breaches into the judicial domain, =
leaving no route of redress.
=20

These are operational and policy failures for which HMCTS and the MoJ bear =
direct responsibility.

Judicial independence cannot be used to shield administrative non-complianc=
e with equality and accessibility obligations.

This situation also reflects a broader failure identified in national polic=
y.

=20

As Tom Purser, CEO of Autism Action, stated in his June 2025 evidence to th=
e House of Lords Autism Act Committee:

=E2=80=9CCrucially we have seen that the Act has not proven to be enforceable at =
any level =E2=80=93 from individuals to ministers =E2=80=93 and no person or agency has =
been made accountable for its delivery or, critically, its failure.=E2=80=9D

=20

My case demonstrates this gap in action. There is currently no accountabili=
ty or enforceability mechanism allowing autistic or otherwise vulnerable cou=
rt users to challenge breaches of Part 3A, the statutory guidance on the Aut=
ism Act 2009 or the Equality Act when the courts themselves fail to comply.

This failure of enforcement leaves disabled litigants without meaningful re=
medy and undermines the integrity of the justice system.

=20

I respectfully request:
Written acknowledgment of this Stage 3 escalation within 48 hours;
A joint review at Permanent-Secretary and Chief-Executive level; and
A substantive response within seven days, as detailed in the attached lette=
r.
=20

Please note that this matter has also been copied to oversight and advocacy=
 recipients for transparency, given its public-interest significance in acce=
ss to justice for neurodivergent and disabled court users.

=20

Yours sincerely,

Nadia Zahmoul

Email: nadia@rosekross.com

Case Nos: CA-2024-001342 / BV20D01752

=20

Attachments
Stage 3 Escalation Letter (30 Oct 2025) and Annex B - Background Note: Misc=
lassification of Equality-Law Breaches as Judicial Matters
Court of Appeal Correspondence (29 Oct 2025, Exhibit NZ-T)
Stage 2 Escalation Letter (29 Oct 2025)
Pre-Action Protocol Letter + Annex A (20 Oct 2025)
Follow-Up Letter (21 Oct 2025)
Urgent Escalation (28 Oct 2025)
Letter to the Autism Act 2009 Committee (24 Oct 2025)
=20

